Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Symmetry for Tensor Network Operations", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"1f877b35-ad02-4079-9223-cad285346b79"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The TensorNetworks paclet's ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "Symmetry"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "efd0ccf0-6e21-4360-8592-965b65f0296a"],
 " subcontext (",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "Wolfram"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "a292ff79-f06b-439d-8c64-e752847a07e5"],
 "TensorNetworks",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "Symmetry"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "8d0b1e4f-8b03-413e-a2f0-11bbe6b01794"],
 "`) exports 12 functions around Young tableaux, the hook-length formula, and \
the Young symmetrizer / projector. Standalone they are pure representation \
theory. Plugged into a tensor network they do three things you cannot do with \
built-in WL alone:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3572cd48-db15-404e-9445-27864c0887e2"],

Cell["\<\
Predict bond multiplicities in closed form, before any tensor is allocated.\
\>", "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"f5686bfc-a07f-4904-a5c6-5d4b0b87e9b1"],

Cell["\<\
Block-diagonalise permutation-symmetric operators along Young irreps.\
\>", "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"7042c427-0be4-4072-8b0b-a7c5c9a6db95"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Enforce multi-term symmetry constraints (e.g. the first Bianchi identity), \
which ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "TensorReduce"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "a56f42ec-1c8f-4482-aa51-da801d39f1b0"],
 " cannot prove from slot-permutation generators."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"50db51eb-975c-4ab1-90be-f03d30729939"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Four runnable examples follow, ordered by how heavily each one leans on the \
Symmetry subcontext. Tier 1 examples sweep over partitions and use ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "TableauDimension"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "61ec1af4-00a4-4bf8-b263-5ac5eeeeccc8"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "HookLengths"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "8ba04c0a-af6c-440b-936b-5d4a052855ef"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "YoungTableau"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "f4e84494-5cc2-4c97-a405-a800ea389129"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "YoungProject"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "2419a086-51c5-490b-8e35-fed9e14d6260"],
 " together. Tier 2 examples make a single, surgical ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "YoungProject"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "d1a6ef4e-0af1-4ca2-9530-a3b8e3dbadb4"],
 " call that cannot be replaced by any built-in canonicalisation."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2befdfc9-4644-47a0-8db6-ea615881379b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every assertion below is verified by ",
 ButtonBox["symmetry_for_tn.wl",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["symmetry_for_tn.wl"], None}],
 " (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"wolframscript", " ", "-", "file"}]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"8336a652-1e01-44ad-8545-92cb0b8ee868"],
 ", all green) and reproduced cell-by-cell in ",
 ButtonBox["SymmetryForTN.nb",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["SymmetryForTN.nb"], None}],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"21f66245-1ef3-41e8-b817-7ee7a0e0f922"],

